  note = {
  CORE ARGUMENT: Gronow examines Kautsky's account of how parliamentary democracy functions as both a terrain of class struggle and a means of socialist transformation, arguing that Kautsky maintained throughout his career that socialist revolution required democratic legitimation through electoral majorities rather than insurrectionary seizure.

  RELEVANCE: This chapter explicates the connection between Kautsky's determinism and his reformist-revolutionary political strategy, showing why his philosophy of history -- which treated capitalism as necessarily generating socialist conditions -- committed him to a parliamentary road.

